<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<suite name="modal_aero_microphysics" version="1.0">
  <!--
    Modal Aerosol Model (MAM4) suite - microphysics block for CAM-SIMA.

    This is the CCPP suite equivalent to existing CAM's
      gas_phase_chemdr -> aero_model_gasaerexch call.
    It contains:
      - setsox (aqueous sulfur chemistry, immediately before the cluster)
      - gasaerexch (gas-aerosol exchange)
      - rename (aerosol mode merging, or renaming)
      - newnuc (new particle nucleation)
      - coag (coagulation)

    Because in CAM it is called within gas_phase_chemdr and is a chemistry/aerosol process,
    the processes below operate on a VMR (molar mixing ratio) array rather than on state%q
    directly.

    The contents of this cluster can be tested using a special snapshot in CAM taken from
    within the chemistry code (not physpkg level), by two methods that are mutually exclusive:

    VMR SOURCE (mutually exclusive method A / method B below):
      A. production shape - use the "mam_vmr_pack" scheme
         mam_vmr_pack converts the injected constituents (mmr) to vmr.
         note that due to this mmr (from snapshot which itself converted from vmr) -> vmr round-trip
         a ~1 ULP diff will be introduced on a distribution-dependent fraction of cells.

      B. bit-for-bit verification - comment out "mam_vmr_pack"; read from snapshot as VMR
         the snapshot's "aerochem_vmr_<name>" fields are updated every time step and are
         bit-for-bit against CAM's vmr (no conversion to mmr on write).

    Init-time ordering:
      mam_constituents        - register aerosol species as CCPP constituents
      sulfur_chemistry_stub   - register the gasaerexch condensable gases (H2SO4, SOAG)
                                as constituents so they read from the snapshot
      mam_mode_metadata       - resolve mode geometry + numptr/lmassptr index maps + the
                                shared specmw/sigmag/spechygro arrays (from const props);
                                sets loffset=0 (the packed-array index contract), so it is
                                provided in both vmr-source methods
      mam_gasaerexch_setup    - resolve gasaerexch gas/aerosol indices + pcage, then call
                                the portable modal_aero_gasaerexch_init (stores module state)
      modal_aero_rename_ccpp  - (init phase) precompute rename coefficients via the portable
                                modal_aero_rename_init. Both mode-merging paths are implemented:
                                the accum-coarse-exchange path (modal_accum_coarse_exch = .true.,
                                the cam6/cam7 FHIST default) resolving 3 pairs, and the no_acc
                                single-pair path; the active path is selected in modal_aero_rename_ccpp

    Run-time ordering:
      tropopause_find  - troplev (strat-sulfate region for gasaerexch + rename)
      mam_mean_mass    - mbar (== mwdry on FHIST) for mmr<->vmr
      mam_vmr_pack     - ccpp_constituents (mmr) -> vmr (molar)
                         [method A only; method B reads vmr from the snapshot]
      mam_vmr_inject_presetsox - [method B only] rewind the member slots to the
                         bit-true pre-setsox capture (P-1); the working array's
                         own ic read lands at P_start = post-setsox
      mam_vmr_checkpoint_entry - save the entry vmr (now PRE-setsox) for the
                         difference unpack, which therefore covers setsox too
                         (CAM's constituent update at the end of
                         aero_model_gasaerexch includes the setsox changes)
      modal_aero_setsox_ccpp - aqueous sulfur chemistry: mutates the working
                         vmr in place (SO2/H2O2/H2SO4 down, cloud-borne
                         so4_c* up)
      mam_setsox_tendency - recover the setsox tendency (vmr - entry)/dt into
                         mam_setsox_vmr_tend, consumed by rename as its
                         dqdt_other/dqqcwdt_other "prior process" tendency
      modal_aero_gasaerexch - condensation/aging: vmr -> dqdt, dotend, qsrflx
      modal_aero_rename_ccpp - mode merging (aitken->accum, plus accum<->coarse when
                               modal_accum_coarse_exch): accumulates onto dqdt, dotend
      mam_vmr_apply    - vmr += dqdt*deltat (CAM's post-rename apply): newnuc
                         and coag consume the updated vmr; also recovers
                         del_h2so4_aeruptk (newnuc input) by bracketing the
                         h2so4 slot around the loop, exactly as CAM does
      modal_aero_newnuc_ccpp - new-particle nucleation: tendency-return,
                               applied to the working vmr by the wrapper
      mam_vmr_checkpoint_postnewnuc - stage vmr for the VERDICT 1 comparison
      modal_aero_coag_ccpp - coagulation: mutates the working vmr IN PLACE
      mam_vmr_checkpoint_postcoag - stage vmr for the VERDICT 2 comparison
      mam_vmr_unpack   - (vmr - vmr_entry)/deltat -> ccpp_constituent_tendencies
                         (difference form: newnuc/coag update vmr directly)
      apply_constituent_tendencies
      (note: no qneg; see below)

    Snapshot inputs (not produced in this suite): dgncur_a, dgncur_awet,
    wetdens, sulfeq, the newnuc met fields (zm, pblh, cld, Q), the setsox
    inputs (invariant oxidant vmr aerochem_vmr_O3/HO2 riding the working
    array's ic read, CO2 via aerochem_co2_mmr, cloud fields cnst_CLDLIQ/
    cnst_NUMLIQ/pbuf_CLD), and mam_del_h2so4_gasprod (from gas-phase
    chemistry). del_h2so4_aeruptk is computed in-suite by mam_vmr_apply - it
    does not exist yet at the "before" capture point, so it cannot be a
    snapshot input. calcsize/calcdry/wateruptake are NOT re-run here; the wet
    cluster has its own suite (modal_aero_wet).

    Note on setsox: setsox runs in-suite (since the P-1 pre-setsox capture);
    its tendency (mam_setsox_vmr_tend) is computed by mam_setsox_tendency as
    (vmr - entry)/dt and consumed by rename as the "other" tendency. Only the
    standalone gasaerexch_rename suite still ic-injects the captured
    mam_setsox_vmr_tend_<name>. Host requirements: MAM aerosol instances
    active (physprop namelist) + setsox_dep_data_file (modal_setsox_nl).
  -->

  <group name="physics_before_coupler">
    <!-- Register MAM aerosol species as CCPP constituents (register phase) -->
    <scheme>mam_constituents</scheme>

    <!-- Register gasaerexch condensable gases (H2SO4, SOAG) as constituents so
         they are read from the snapshot; the aerosols come from mam_constituents -->
    <scheme>sulfur_chemistry_stub</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: mode metadata + species index maps -->
    <scheme>mam_mode_metadata</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: chemistry vmr workspace membership (solved / invariant /
         none per constituent slot; drives pack/unpack/inject/tendency) -->
    <scheme>chem_vmr_metadata</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: resolve gasaerexch indices + pcage, call portable gasaerexch init -->
    <scheme>mam_gasaerexch_setup</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: wv_sat_init (newnuc computes relative humidity via qsat) -->
    <scheme>to_be_ccppized_temporary</scheme>

    <!-- Tropopause level for the stratospheric-sulfate region -->
    <scheme>tropopause_find</scheme>

    <!-- Gas-aerosol exchange cluster -->
    <scheme>mam_mean_mass</scheme>

    <!-- vmr source: methods A and B are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE - keep exactly one
         active (comment the other out). See the header comment. -->
    <!-- method A: production shape - pack the injected constituents (mmr) to vmr. -->
    <!-- <scheme>mam_vmr_pack</scheme> -->
    <!-- method B: certification - no pack; vmr is read from the snapshot's raw
         aerochem_vmr_<name> fields via the registry (bit-true CAM vmr inputs).
         Activate by commenting out mam_vmr_pack above. -->

    <!-- method B only: rewind the member slots of the working vmr to the
         bit-true pre-setsox boundary (P-1 capture); comment out under
         method A (production shape: the packed pre-setsox constituents ARE
         the entry state) -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_inject_presetsox</scheme>

    <!-- Cluster-entry checkpoint: save the entry vmr (pre-setsox) for the
         setsox tendency and the difference unpack at the end -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_checkpoint_entry</scheme>

    <!-- Aqueous sulfur chemistry: mutates the working vmr in place -->
    <scheme>modal_aero_setsox_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=setsox_sub -->

    <!-- Recover the setsox tendency (vmr - entry)/dt for rename's
         dqdt_other/dqqcwdt_other -->
    <scheme>mam_setsox_tendency</scheme>

    <scheme>modal_aero_gasaerexch</scheme>
    <scheme>modal_aero_rename_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=modal_aero_rename_run -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_apply</scheme>

    <!-- New-particle nucleation: tendency-return, applied to the working vmr
         by the wrapper -->
    <scheme>modal_aero_newnuc_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=modal_aero_newnuc_run -->

    <!-- VERDICT 1: stage the post-newnuc state for the ncdata_check
         comparison against aerochem_vmr_postnewnuc -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_checkpoint_postnewnuc</scheme>

    <!-- Coagulation: init phase builds the pair tables and calls the portable
         modal_aero_coag_init; run phase mutates the working vmr in place -->
    <scheme>modal_aero_coag_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=modal_aero_coag_run -->

    <!-- VERDICT 2: stage the post-coag state for the ncdata_check comparison
         against aerochem_vmr_postcoag -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_checkpoint_postcoag</scheme>

    <!-- Unpack the cluster's total change, (vmr - vmr_entry)/deltat, into
         ccpp_constituent_tendencies for the framework apply below (difference
         form because newnuc applies its tendency wrapper-internally and coag
         updates vmr in place). This is the production shape under method A;
         under method B the constituents evolve in parallel and are not the
         verdict - the vmr-space checkpoints above are the b4b gates. -->
    <scheme>mam_vmr_unpack</scheme>

    <!-- Apply the gas-aerosol exchange constituent tendencies -->
    <scheme>apply_constituent_tendencies</scheme>

    <!-- note: intentionally no qneg here as constituent tendency applier in CAM is not part of the snapshot clamp. -->
    <!-- <scheme>qneg</scheme> -->
  </group>
</suite>
